yoyo todo and yoyo goal on the shell now print shell commands (yoyo todo add <description>, yoyo goal set <desc>) instead of the REPL's slash commands. Committed as 6e1ff439, titled "Part of #1086". cargo build, cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

Probe counts (empty temp dir, bare and zz1 zz2 zz3, lines containing /<verb>):

| Verb | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| goal | 9 | 0 |
| todo | 11 | 2 |

What changed
• The surface (REPL or shell) is passed in as an argument, not a global. The shell dispatcher passes the shell form; the REPL entry points pass the REPL form.
• This covers the todo board messages and goal's set and verify messages too, not just the usage tables.
• REPL output is byte-identical: tests compare the full todo usage, board usage and goal unknown-subcommand text against the old strings.
• Exit codes were checked before and after and haven't changed: todo bare 0 / unknown 2, goal bare 0 / unknown 2, goal set 0.

Decisions to know about
• `goal check` only works inside a session. The shell refusal now reads "yoyo goal check needs an interactive session." and still ends "Start yoyo and use: /goal check". The shell usage table marks that row "(interactive session only)".
• The 2 remaining todo lines are on purpose. They're the same line, once per probe call: the session note now ends "start yoyo and use: /todo". The todo list only exists inside a session, so the slash command is the right thing to name there. The shell-output test allows /<verb> only right after "yoyo and use: " (the wording the existing refusals already use). I've offered the other option, dropping the slash form from that note, on #1086.
• Not touched: yoyo goal set with no description still exits 0, as it did before. That's a #982-type question, so I left it out of this change.

Tests: I added seven rows for todo and goal to the shell-output test. To check they catch the bug, I temporarily switched the shell calls back to the REPL form; the test failed by name, and passed again once restored. I ran that twice, once for both commands and once for goal alone.

I also updated docs/src/usage/commands.md, which said unknown-verb usage text was "unchanged". handle_goal and the board helper that takes a directory are now test-only because nothing else calls them, and I removed the unused handle_todo_board wrapper.

Still on #1086 (posted there with the counts and commit id): grep 10, map 2, index 2, blame 1, lint 1, risk 1, skill 1, plus the yoyo help doctor text. grep is most of what's left, but commands_search.rs is already 20 lines over its size limit (4593 vs 4573), so that file needs room before the grep slice can go in.
